# What pacman says when the console is installed, upgraded or removed.
#
# These functions run as ROOT, at package time, possibly in a chroot, with no
# idea which human this machine belongs to and no session to talk to. So they
# do nothing at all except print. Every per-user step -- enabling the user
# service, the Omarchy template, the hook and the menu entries -- is
# `toon-console-install`, run by the person whose keys and whose ~/.config
# these are.
#
# In particular nothing here touches ~/.local/share/toon-console. An upgrade
# and a removal leave the account's data directory, its Lease Vault cache and
# its keystore exactly as they were, because nothing in this package ever
# names them.

post_install() {
  cat <<'MESSAGE'

  The TOON Console is installed. One command, as yourself, wires it up:

      toon-console-install

  That enables toon-console.service for your user and starts it, and -- on
  Omarchy -- installs the themed template, the theme-set hook, the three menu
  entries and a post-update hook. Then launch "TOON Console" (SUPER + SPACE),
  or run `toon-console`.

  It writes only under your $HOME. Run it once per account that uses the
  console; it is safe to run again at any time.

MESSAGE
}

post_upgrade() {
  cat <<'MESSAGE'

  The TOON Console has been upgraded. pacman cannot restart a user service,
  so a console that is running is still running the previous build:

      systemctl --user daemon-reload
      systemctl --user try-restart toon-console.service

  On Omarchy the post-update hook does both on the next `omarchy update`, and
  re-applies the desktop integration from this package. Your data directory
  (~/.local/share/toon-console) has not been touched.

MESSAGE
}

pre_remove() {
  cat <<'MESSAGE'

  Before this package goes: take the per-user half out too, as yourself --

      toon-console-uninstall

  It stops and disables the user service, and removes the Omarchy template,
  the hooks and the menu entries from your ~/.config. (`toon-console-install`
  left a copy of it in ~/.local/bin, so it still works afterwards.)

  It does NOT remove ~/.local/share/toon-console, and neither does pacman:
  your channel state, Lease Vault cache and keystore survive both.

MESSAGE
}
